---
import '../styles/global.css';
import {chapters} from '../curriculum/chapters';
import {systemsChapters} from '../curriculum/systems-chapters';
import {sitePath} from '../lib/site-path';
const sortedSys=[...systemsChapters].sort((a,b)=>Number(a.number)-Number(b.number));
const groups=[...new Set(sortedSys.map(c=>c.group))];
---
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><title>Precision through digital · The Analog Notebook</title><meta name="description" content="A learning path through precision measurement, power, RF, transmission lines, data converters and digital communication."/></head><body>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="topbar"><a class="brand" href={sitePath('/')}>∿ the analog notebook.</a><span class="edition">FROM MEASUREMENT TO COMMUNICATION</span><a class="top-link" href={sitePath('/opamp-coverage/')}>Op-amp foundations ↗</a></header>
<div class="book-shell"><aside class="sidebar"><a class="course-label" href={sitePath('/')}>FOUNDATIONS <span>{chapters.length} CHAPTERS</span></a><p class="sidebar-title">Precision through digital</p><nav aria-label="Topic groups">{groups.map((g,i)=><a href={`#group-${i}`}>{g}</a>)}</nav></aside><main id="main"><div class="chapter-hero"><div class="eyebrow">SYSTEMS TOPIC GUIDE</div><h1>Precision through digital<br/><em>Follow the signal and the energy.</em></h1><p class="dek">Build accurate measurements, power them, carry fast signals and turn voltages into information. Each chapter combines physical intuition, derivations, operating-point examples, practical notes and an independent practice notebook.</p></div><p>The op-amp chapters establish feedback, noise, stability and precision functions. This path extends those ideas to complete systems. RF and transmission lines come before fast converter and communication interfaces so that edge rates, reflections, return paths and common-mode behavior have a physical explanation.</p>
{groups.map((g,i)=><section id={`group-${i}`}><div class="section-heading"><span>{i+1}</span><h2>{g}</h2></div><div class="systems-cards">{sortedSys.filter(c=>c.group===g).map(c=><article><span class="tiny-label">CHAPTER {c.number}</span><h3><a href={sitePath(c.href)}>{c.title}</a></h3><p>{c.sections.slice(1,-1).map(s=>s[1]).join(' · ')}</p><a href={sitePath(c.practice)}>Three independent problems →</a></article>)}</div></section>)}<p>Use the synthesis case at the end of each reading to compare three operating conditions. A correct nominal calculation becomes a useful design only after the limiting conditions, component tolerances and measurement method are specified.</p></main></div><footer class="footer"><span>The Analog Notebook · Original teaching material</span></footer></body></html>
<style>.systems-cards{display:grid;gap:1.3rem}.systems-cards article{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:1.4rem}.systems-cards h3{margin:.6rem 0}.systems-cards p{font-size:.9rem}</style>
